Run fwts tests in the uefi category (as returned by fwts --uefitests).
These run automatically by default and require no user intervention.

This includes the following tests (based on x86_64, may vary on other arches):

csm             UEFI Compatibility Support Module test.
esrt            Sanity check UEFI ESRT Table.
securebootcert  UEFI secure boot test.
uefibootpath    Sanity check for UEFI Boot Path Boot####.
uefirtauthvar   Authenticated variable tests.
uefirtmisc      UEFI miscellaneous runtime service interface tests.
uefirttime      UEFI Runtime service time interface tests.
uefirtvariable  UEFI Runtime service variable interface tests.

On aarch64 it currently skips the following unsafe tests:
uefirtauthvar uefirtmisc uefirttime uefirtvariable

https://wiki.ubuntu.com/Kernel/Reference/fwts

Note:

All tests other than csm will abort on a non-UEFI enabled machine. Uefirt*
tests may oops, panic or reboot the system on certain implementations.
